  "description_html": "<section aria-labelledby=\"courseDescription\">\n    ACTS Common Course - MATH 1113.\n\nCorequisite: Students not meeting the below prerequisite will enroll in MATH 0803. \n\nPrerequisite: Score of 19 or above on the math section of the ACTE; score of 500 or above on the math section of RSAT; score of 250 or above on the arithmetic section or quantitative reasoning, algebra, and statistics section of ACCUPLACER; or earn a grade of C* or higher in MATH 0803 or MATH 0903 or TMAT 1203.\n\nCo-requisite: Students not meeting the above prerequisite, will enroll in MATH 1003 and the co-requisite MATH 0803.\n\nThis quantitative literacy course focuses upon the mathematics of contemporary life. Topics include using and understanding number quantities and measurement, statistics, probability, finances (personal, state and national), and mathematical modeling. \n\nNote: A grade of C of better must be earned in this course if being used to satisfy the general education mathematics requirement.\n    \n</section>",
